{
  "id": "surface-and-contour-duality",
  "title": "Surface ↔ Contour: One Hill, Two Views",
  "eyebrow": "level curves",
  "language": "en",
  "duration": 48,
  "topic": "A 2D contour plot encodes a 3D surface. Sweeping a horizontal cutting plane up through z=f(x,y) traces level curves on the surface; project them straight down to the xy-plane to get the contour map. Tight contours mean steep slopes.",
  "subject_id": "mat2b",
  "chapter_number": 5,
  "prerequisites": [],
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "manimoIntro",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 5.88,
      "narration": "How do you draw a hill on a flat page? A contour map. Let us see why it works.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "center",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "manimo-enter",
            "content": "Manimo enters centre",
            "delay": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "One hill, two views.",
            "delay": 0.7,
            "color": "var(--chalk-100)",
            "position": "right of Manimo, serif italic"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "setup",
      "start": 5.88,
      "end": 15,
      "narration": "Here is the hill — a surface z equals f of x and y. Below it, a blank xy plane, ready to receive its shadow.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "left-right",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Oblique 3D axes and surface wireframe",
            "delay": 0.3,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "f(x, y) = 1.2 − 0.3 x² − 0.2 y²",
            "delay": 1.4,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "near surface"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Empty contour plot pane (axes only)",
            "delay": 2,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "the xy plane — waiting for level curves",
            "delay": 3,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)",
            "position": "below contour pane"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sweep",
      "start": 15,
      "end": 29.21,
      "narration": "Slice the surface with a horizontal plane at height h. The cross section is a closed curve — the level set. Drop it straight down to the floor and you have one contour. Sweep h upward and the contour map fills in.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "left-right",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Horizontal cutting plane at z=h, sweeping upward",
            "delay": 0.4,
            "color": "var(--teal-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Highlighted intersection ellipse on the surface",
            "delay": 0.6,
            "color": "var(--amber-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Dashed projection lines from intersection down to the xy-plane",
            "delay": 1,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)"
          },
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Contour curve drawn in the xy-pane in sync with the plane height",
            "delay": 1.2,
            "color": "var(--amber-400)"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-formula",
            "content": "f(x, y) = h",
            "delay": 2,
            "color": "var(--amber-300)",
            "position": "right panel"
          },
          {
            "type": "text-caption",
            "content": "every height becomes a level curve below",
            "delay": 3.4,
            "color": "var(--chalk-300)",
            "position": "right panel sub-caption"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "spacing",
      "start": 29.21,
      "end": 37.36,
      "narration": "Tight contours, steep slope. Loose contours, gentle slope. The map reads height changes from line spacing.",
      "visuals": {
        "layout": "left-right",
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "svg-path",
            "content": "Full contour map (all levels persistent)",
            "delay": 0,
